cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use kusim in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "kusim: a 3-D two-phase (oil/water) IMPES reservoir simulator in Python for teaching and history matching"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24144332   # concept DOI: always resolves to the latest release
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24144333
    description: "Archived release v0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MElfeel/kusim"
url: "https://github.com/MElfeel/kusim"
abstract: >-
  kusim is a 3-D, two-phase (oil/water) reservoir simulator in Python, ported from a legacy FORTRAN
  IMPES code and written to be read. It can be used as a Python library, from the command line with
  JSON files (for scripts and LLM agents), and as the basis for history matching and optimisation
  with ensemble methods (ES-MDA, EnKF) and hand-written adjoint gradients.
keywords:
  - reservoir simulation
  - IMPES
  - two-phase flow
  - history matching
  - ensemble methods
  - adjoint
  - Python
authors:
